    "narrative": "The **Gunnar Henderson** and **Jackson Merrill** tandem anchors the Austin Waves lineup today, representing our most potent scoring threats against favorable matchups. **Gunnar Henderson** boasts an elite 83.29 score, benefiting from a high-leverage order position and an advantageous platoon split against the right-handed L\u00f3pez, while **Jackson Merrill** capitalizes on the struggling Junk, whose 4.58 xERA provides the runway for a 71.41 performance. Behind them, **Drake Baldwin** earns a prime 72.68 rating; his aggressive lead-off spot combined with a friendly park factor and a 0.386 xwOBA confirms him as a must-start asset in our quest to bolster run production.\n\nTactically, we are leaning into specific environmental edges to maximize our efficiency. **Denzer Guzman** (53.14) receives a significant boost from an \"out\" wind forecast, mitigating the hurdle of a tough southpaw, while **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (69.74) remains a core play despite facing a pitcher with a 3.58 xERA, largely due to his resilience against left-handed offerings. Our closest bench decision involved **Jorge Polanco**, who hovered at a 45.79 rating; ultimately, he was sidelined because his matchup against the 3.67 xERA of Sheehan provided insufficient upside compared to the higher-floor profiles of **Dominic Smith** and **Andy Pages**.\n\nWhile the board looks favorable, managers should note the risk profile surrounding **Heliot Ramos** (56.33). Though his wind-aided score is acceptable, his high SB potential is muted by an elite opposing battery, which suppresses his projected stolen base output. Additionally, keep a watchful eye on **Liam Hicks** (55.00); while his SP skill adjustment is positive against Buehler, his lower base projection leaves him as a marginal start. Ensure all lineup slots are monitored for late-breaking weather shifts, as these marginal plays are the first candidates for benching should conditions deteriorate.",
